        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find out what happens for the three-digit multiples of 37 below:\n\n$185,\\ 259,\\ 296,\\ 740,\\ 814$ and $925$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Every clockwise rotation is also a multiple of 37, including $074=74$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}185&=5\\times37\\\\851&=23\\times37\\\\518&=14\\times37\\\\259&=7\\times37\\\\592&=16\\times37\\\\925&=25\\times37\\\\296&=8\\times37\\\\962&=26\\times37\\\\629&=17\\times37\\\\740&=20\\times37\\\\407&=11\\times37\\\\074&=2\\times37\\\\814&=22\\times37\\\\148&=4\\times37\\\\481&=13\\times37\\end{align*}$$\nThe rotations of 925 are 925, 259 and 592, already checked above. In every case, all clockwise rotations are multiples of 37. A leading zero is retained when recording the rotation, but $074$ has value $74$.",
